WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
- All right, I have one last story I found

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.257
that made me smile.

00:00:03.257 --> 00:00:04.380
Hopefully you'll feel the same.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.454
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.454 --> 00:00:08.700
(upbeat music)
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.320
I don't care what age you are,

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.110
every person deserves to
have love, companionship

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.060
and frankly, a little pampering.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.560
That's exactly what a New York woman

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.630
is promoting with her group, Glamour Gals.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.360
For the past two decades,
she's recruited teens

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.310
to join her at senior homes.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.780
They hang out with the residents

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.600
while also doing their nails,
their hair, little makeovers

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.600
that make everybody feel
beautiful on the inside and out.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.010
It's nice.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.600
We have the founder of Glamour Gals

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.270
on the line right now
watching on NBC New York.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.230
What's up Rachel?
(audience applauding)

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.129
- Hi, Kelly! Hi!

00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:40.962
- Hi!

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.250
I actually used to do
this with my church group.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.083
Whenever I was a kid,

00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:46.770
we used to do something similar to this

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.300
and that's how it was introduced to me.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.130
But where did you come up with the idea?

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:53.220
- It's actually in honor
of my own grandmother.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.460
I wanted to give her a beauty makeover,

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.620
but she lived in a senior
home across the country

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.690
and it just never happened.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.810
So when she passed away,
I wanted to honor her

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.890
and so I had this idea of
going into my local senior home

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.290
and providing beauty
makeovers to the residents

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.460
who live there.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.460
To sit down, to connect, to
share a compliment and a story

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.100
and just make someone feel
loved and appreciated.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.140
And it was actually at my first makeover,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.110
I had two friends, just
two friends show up,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.960
but from there, two decades later,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.860
we've inspired thousands of
teen volunteers to do the same

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.040
and it's as valuable to them as it's to us

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.010
and everybody we serve.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.750
- Yeah, absolutely.
(audience applauding)

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.720
So you have a special
holiday project, right?

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.590
- That's right.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.940
Absolutely.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:48.570
Our My Dear Friend Card
Writing Campaign wants to reach

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.790
as many seniors as possible.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.850
Anyone can write holiday notes, even kids,

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.090
and we pair them with
seniors around the country.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.960
Our goal is to reach
30,000 isolated seniors

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.180
with cards this holiday seasons.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.310
So please get writing.
- That's so cool.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.210
I love that.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.440
Even the pen pal thing in general

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.070
and I even love how a
kid with a grandparent

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.980
kind of aged person,
that's a really cool thing

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.150
just to see what would cultivate

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.070
from that kind of relationship.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.930
That's a super cool idea.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.060
Thank you so much.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.390
If you wanna be part of
My Dear Friend Cards,

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.970
check out our Insta story for info.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.050
You gotta check that out everybody.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.100
Thank you so much for Rachel.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.540
What a beautiful thing you're doing.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.373
- Thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:02:31.373 --> 00:02:33.411
I'm liking your posts right now, okay?

00:02:33.411 --> 00:02:34.244
(bell dinging)

00:02:34.244 --> 00:02:36.240
And that's not all our
season long partner Pilot Pen

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.670
makers of G2, the go-to pen
at "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.670
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, ma'am.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.800
So they're gonna be writing Glamour Gals

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.210
a check for a thousand dollars.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.043
How's that sound?
(audience applauding)

00:02:46.043 --> 00:02:50.715
- Oh my gosh!
- That'll help some supplies.

00:02:50.715 --> 00:02:52.950
- So much!
- Absolutely.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:56.177
Thank you Rachel and thank you
to all our guests this hour,

00:02:56.177 --> 00:03:00.270
Ubah Hassan, Erin Lichy,
Matt Rogers, Maestro Kyso,

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.470
and Jeff Kinney and Jacob.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.370
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

